      "note": "Kāf-Hā-Yā-ʿAyn-Ṣād. Dhikru raḥmati rabbika ʿabdahū zakariyyā, idh nādā rabbahū nidāʾan khafiyyā (2–3). Wa kānati mraʾatī ʿāqiran fa-hab lī min ladunka waliyyā (5). Yā zakariyyā innā nubashshiruka bi-ghulāmini smuhū yaḥyā, lam najʿal lahū min qablu samiyyā (7). Qāla kadhālika qāla rabbuka huwa ʿalayya hayyin (9). Note: the poster's sanctuary and Maryam's provision come from Aal Imran 3:37–38 ('whenever Zakariyya entered upon her in the miḥrāb he found provision with her… there Zakariyya called on his Lord'); Surah Maryam itself only says he called 'in secret'."
