      "note": "Ḍaraba lakum mathalan min anfusikum: hal lakum mimmā malakat aymānukum min shurakāʾa fī mā razaqnākum fa-antum fīhi sawāʾ, takhāfūnahum ka-khīfatikum anfusakum (28) — 'He gives you an example from yourselves: do your slaves share equally in what We have provided you, so that you fear them as you fear one another?'; bali ttabaʿa lladhīna ẓalamū ahwāʾahum bi-ghayri ʿilm (29) — 'rather, the wrongdoers follow their desires without knowledge'. Checked: the poster's argument — people refuse to treat servants as equal owners, yet make equals of Allah — is the 30:28 mathal; 'followed desires without knowledge' is 30:29."
