      "note": "Alif Lām Mīm. Ghulibati r-Rūm (2) — 'the Romans have been defeated' — fī adnā l-arḍi wa hum min baʿdi ghalabihim sa-yaghlibūn (3) — 'in the nearest land; and after their defeat they will prevail' — fī biḍʿi sinīn (4) — 'within a few years'. Checked: 'the empire appears finished' is 30:2–3; the words 'a few years' (biḍʿ, three to nine) fit the poster's 'years pass'. Note: the verses name only ar-Rūm; the victorious enemy being Persia and the painted word 'FINISHED' are the poster's context and image, not words of the surah."
