      "note": "A-wa lam yasīrū fi l-arḍi fa-yanẓurū kayfa kāna ʿāqibatu lladhīna min qablihim, kānū ashadda minhum quwwatan wa athārū l-arḍa wa ʿamarūhā akthara mimmā ʿamarūhā… fa-mā kāna llāhu li-yaẓlimahum wa lākin kānū anfusahum yaẓlimūn (9) — 'they were stronger, they tilled the earth and built on it more than these; but Allah did not wrong them — they wronged themselves'. Checked: the poster's plaque is 30:9; 'taller towers, richer farms, larger armies' is the poster's expansion of 'stronger… tilled… built'."
